>>Q000628 036 
#tr.en: On the river, on the river, like sailing (on the) river - like the spouse sweet, like the town sweet, such a sweet (thing) does not exist! - 
37. i7-de3 i7-nun-e i7-diri-gin7 
>>Q000628 037 
#tr.en: On the river, on the Prince-canal, like sailing (on the) river. 
38. i7-de3 {i7}buranun-na i7-diri-gin7 
>>Q000628 038 
#tr.en: On the river, on the Euphrates, like sailing (on the) river. 
39. i7-{i7}buranun-na-ke4 i7-diri-gin7 
>>Q000628 039 
#tr.en: On the course of the Euphrates, like sailing (on the) river. 
40. sza3? e2?-dim3?-ma?-sze3? im?-da?-gen?-na?-gin7? 
>>Q000628 040 
#tr.en: Like she(?) went to(?) the center(?) of Edim(?). 
41. dim3?-me?-er mu-lu im?-da-gen-na-gin7 (x) 
>>Q000628 041 
#tr.en: Like the deity of man(kind) went with her(?). 
42. dam-gin7 ze2-eb uru2-gin7 ze2-eb ur5-gin7 ze2-eb nu-gal2 
>>Q000628 042 
#tr.en: Like the spouse sweet, like the town sweet, such a sweet (thing) does not exist! 
43. {d}am-an-ki am-uru2-ze2-ba im-da-gen-na-gin7 (x) 
>>Q000628 043 
#tr.en: Like Enki, the wild bull of the sweet town, went with her(?). 
44. ama?-e2-mah-a {d}dam-gal-nun-na im-da-gen-na-gin7 (x) 
>>Q000628 044 
#tr.en: Like the mother of the Emah, Damgalnuna, went with her(?). 
45. {d}asar-lu2-hi dumu-uru2-ze2-ba im-da-gen-na-gin7 
>>Q000628 045 
#tr.en: Like Asarluḫi, the child of the sweet town, went with her(?). 
46. {d}mu-ul-lil2-le mu-un-gu7-a-gin7 mu-un-nag-a-gin7 dam-gin7 ze2-eb uru2-gin7 ze2-eb ur5-gin7 ze2-eb nu-gal2 
>>Q000628 046 
#tr.en: Like Enlil ate (and) like he drank - like the spouse sweet, like the town sweet, such a sweet (thing) does not exist! 
47. SZA3? x NE ne-en sza3-mu ba-ma-al 
>>Q000628 047 
#tr.en: (...) my heart is placed. 
48. a lu2-zi!-de3 szu e-ba-sze3 
>>Q000628 048 
#tr.en: To the house(?) where the righteous man raised (his) hand. 
49. a-bi lu2-zi-de3 szu bi2-in-e3-ba-a-sze3 
>>Q000628 049 
#tr.en: To that house(?) where the righteous man raised (his) hand. 
50. mu-lu-bi e2-sza3-ga {mu}nu2 gi-rin-ne bi2-in-ak 
>>Q000628 050 
#tr.en: In the Ešag that man set up a bed in flowers. 
51. e2-an-na-ka gada-la2-e! na ba-e-na-ag2 
>>Q000628 051 
#tr.en: In the House-of-Heaven the linen-clad erected(?) a stone(?) for him. 
52. u3-mu-un-ra a mu-un-ma-al mu-na-ab-be2-ne 
