#tr.en: They are telling him to refresh in the palace. 
55. {d}dumu-zi e2-e-am3 ki-am3 u4-zalag-ga 
>>Q000628 055 
#tr.en: O Dumuzi, it is in(?) the house, a place bright as a day it is. 
56. ama {d}inanna ama {d}inanna du6-zu du-zu 
>>Q000628 056 
#tr.en: Mother Inanna, Mother Inanna, your hill(?), your going(?). 
57. ama {d}inanna {d}inanna-an-na tug2-zu tug2-zu 
>>Q000628 057 
#tr.en: Mother Inanna, Inanna-of-Heaven, your clothes, your clothes. 
58. tug2-gi6-zu tug2-babbar-zu 
>>Q000628 058 
#tr.en: Your black clothes, your white clothes. 
59. mu-lu e2-a gen-na-mu te-e-am3 
>>Q000628 059 
#tr.en: It is indeed(?) my man who strolled around the house. 
60. i-lu te-am3 ad-sza4-sza3-ba 
>>Q000628 060 
#tr.en: It is indeed(?) a song, a heart’s lament. 
61. me-e-bi te-am3 me ba-tusz-u3-ne 
>>Q000628 061 
#tr.en: Its me it is indeed. They (shall) place the me. 
62. ki-bi te-am3 ki am3-gub-bu-ne 
>>Q000628 062 
